Glory of Rome <version>
=======================

Glory of Rome has been a turn-based fantasy strategy game: raise an army,
hunt the villains who have carved up Italia, and deliver them to the Senate
before your commission runs out. It has run on OpenBounty, an open-source
engine, and everything it needs has been in this folder -- there has been
nothing else to download.


INSTALL

  Linux:    extract the tarball and run ./openbounty
  Windows:  extract the zip and double-click openbounty.exe
  macOS:    extract the zip; Gatekeeper has blocked the first launch.
            Right-click openbounty in Finder, choose Open, then click
            Open in the dialog. Or, from a terminal:
              xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ./openbounty

  Keep the assets folder next to the program: the game has been in it.


CONTROLS

  Arrow keys or the numeric keypad have moved; Enter has chosen; Esc has
  opened the game menu, where every command lives. A gamepad has worked
  too.


MORE

  Source, issues and releases: https://github.com/dannyheskett/openbounty
